-- title:
--   Non-toric finite p-points have non-zero abelian-quotient coordinates
-- statement:
--   Fix a non-zero $N_0$ and a prime $p$ with $p \nmid N_0$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $p$ a non-unit of $A$ (so $A$ lies over $p$), and a level datum $\Lambda$ of type `LevelData N₀ p A`: a morphism $\sigma_A \colon \operatorname{Spec} A \to \operatorname{Spec}$ of the localisation of $\mathbb Z$ at $p$ restricting along `barPt A` to the generic point, a scheme $X$ with structure morphism $f$ to that base, a relative group law on $f$, and bijections $\Lambda.\mathrm{pts}$ from $J_0(N_0) =$ `JZero N₀` onto the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-points of $f$ and $\Lambda.\mathrm{ptsSp}$ from `JZeroC (ResidueField A) N₀` onto the points of $f$ over $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the residue field $\kappa$ of $A$; $h\Lambda$ asserts `Λ.IsJacobian`, i.e. that $f$ carries the abelian-scheme property bundle, the group law is commutative, $\Lambda.\mathrm{pts}$ and $\Lambda.\mathrm{ptsSp}$ are additive, $\Lambda.\mathrm{pts}$ is Galois-equivariant, reduction of points agrees mod $\ell$ whenever the reduction inputs hold, and every Hecke operator is realised by an endomorphism of $f$. Let $O$ be a Néron object of type `JZeroNeronObjectAtP N₀ p hpN₀ A hA Λ`: a smooth, separated, locally of finite type, quasi-compact, surjective morphism $g \colon G \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathbb Z_{(p)}$ with preconnected fibres, a commutative relative group law with flat surjective multiplication-by-$n$ maps and proper generic fibre, an additive Galois-equivariant bijection $O.\mathrm{pts}$ from $J_0(N_0p)$ onto the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-points of $g$, a Hecke action, a toric rank and the remaining structure fields (including the morphisms $O.\mathrm{abqFibre}\,i$ from the base change of $g$ to $\kappa$ to that of $f$). Let $x \in J_0(N_0p)$ lie in `O.finPts p`, the subgroup generated by the $p$-torsion points admitting an $A$-valued extension, suppose both degeneracy pushforwards `degeneracyPushforwardPair N₀ p 0` and `degeneracyPushforwardPair N₀ p 1` (pushforward along the two degeneracy inclusions, or $0$ if the required integrality, finiteness and norm inputs fail) kill $x$, and suppose $x \notin$ `O.toricPts p`, the subgroup generated by the toric points of level $p$. Let $s$ be a point of $g$ over $\sigma_A$ whose restriction along `barPt A` is the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-point $O.\mathrm{pts}\,x$. Then, writing $\bar s$ for the composite of `resPt A` with $s$, at least one of the two elements $\Lambda.\mathrm{ptsSp}^{-1}(\mathrm{fibreMap}\,(O.\mathrm{abqFibre}\,i)\,\bar s)$ of `JZeroC (ResidueField A) N₀`, for $i = 0$ and $i = 1$, is non-zero.
--
--   This is the step in Ribet's analysis of the special fibre at $p$ of the Néron model of $J_0(N_0p)$ which says that a point of the finite part annihilated by both degeneracy pushforwards and lying outside the toric part has non-trivial image in one of the two abelian-quotient factors; the counting input is the comparison of $p^{\mathrm{toricRank}}$ with the cardinality of the toric subgroup. It is used in the derivation of lower-level torsion and of the non-vanishing of the Hecke-stable torsion subgroup from such a non-toric point.
